<title>VENEZUELA: RTRS - CRA-RTZ qualify to bid in Venezuela aluminium.</title>
<headline>RTRS - CRA-RTZ qualify to bid in Venezuela aluminium.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>sector sale</p>
<p>The Venezuelan Investment Fund announced (FIV) on Wednesday that 13 companies, including RTZ-CRA, had qualified to bid for a controlling interest in Venezuela's four-company aluminum sector later this year.</p>
<p>The list of interested bidders for smelters Alcasa and Venalum, carbon anode producer Carbonorca and bauxite and alumina producer Bauxilum includes top aluminum companies from the United States, Australia and Japan.</p>
<p>Apart from RTZ-CRA, the companies that have qualified for the privatization are: Alumax Inc, Aluminum Co of America, Gencor Ltd, Glencore Ltd, Reynolds Metals Co, Kaiser Aluminum Corp, Ormet Corporation/Alentuy, Norsk Hydro ASA, Alcan Aluminum Ltd, Mitsubishi Metals Corp, Sural and Marubeni.</p>
<p>Analysts say the four companies, which include Venalum's 430,000 tonnes per year capacity smelter, are worth about $2 billion.</p>
<p>-- Caracas Newsroom, 582 505 2600</p>
</text>
